The solution checker is run with a single argument, the root directory of the set of instances. A .bat file is provided for windows and a shell-script is available for linux. In the scripts, you may have to change the pathname of the root directory of the set of instances. \
The solution checker is written in java and requires a java 7 version (of course java 8 would also be OK).\
/instances_directory\uc0\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 list_instances.csv\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 /instance1\u8232 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 /instance2\u8232 The file \'ab\'a0list_instances.csv\'a0\'bb contains the list of instances to check. The checker expects to find input and results files in each instance directory (as shown below).\
